From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/meson-gpio: pass irq_set_wake to the parent

The GPIO interrupt controller had no irq_set_wake and no
IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE, so enable_irq_wake() on any GPIO interrupt
failed with -ENXIO. Drivers that ignore that error then warn
"Unbalanced IRQ wake disable" on resume.

On the ODROID-GO Ultra both PMICs (RK817 with the power key and its
RTC, RK818 with the charger) signal through GPIO interrupts. In
suspend-to-idle the kernel disables every interrupt that is not armed
for wakeup, so nothing could wake the board: it slept until power was
cut. Pass the call to the parent (the GIC skips it), as other
hierarchical GPIO interrupt controllers do; s2idle now wakes on the
RTC alarm (IRQ 17, RK817).

---
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-meson-gpio.c
@@ -535,6 +535,7 @@
 	.irq_eoi		= irq_chip_eoi_parent,
 	.irq_set_type		= meson_gpio_irq_set_type,
 	.irq_retrigger		= irq_chip_retrigger_hierarchy,
+	.irq_set_wake		= irq_chip_set_wake_parent,
 #ifdef CONFIG_SMP
 	.irq_set_affinity	= irq_chip_set_affinity_parent,
 #endif
